{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994012868786001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"main-name-crowd","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Joe Oakhart","head_sha":"c6604405876bc4ea7004918052ce6cd02be5b4ec","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: 9322-f84a-e047-4471","material: bbb765ba0e895e74","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 3","regver: bb57585159a067c5","verified-at-sha:c6604405876bc4ea7004918052ce6cd02be5b4ec"],"signature":"f81db3b6c2860225e45ff63b807eabf19d2a2ae9f4e091b2a2d0b835f1ed84b1","signed_at":1783105533738973000}},"author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":9},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"519f9563d289e54ff50188973556f881ff41c0e904da2a8bfcc7737537000754","event_uuid":"e36af9a5-f48c-4903-a9d9-456ba62cbf02","position":{"commit_sha":"542f13119aad284ba8ef8574e57f4d258cb43541","position":"1785007192460120001-e36af9a5-f48c-4903-a9d9-456ba62cbf02"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"DECISION: item 8 (module-size allowlist governance) REJECTED. Requiring human review on the allowlist adds too much friction for a soft code-quality gate. Chosen approach: the allowlist stays a RECORD, remediated periodically through maintenance sessions (like this audit). No ratchet / CODEOWNERS-gate / merge-base delta check. Item 9 (import-cycle SCC) APPROVED — all 3 sub-remediations.","timestamp":1783057918432225001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"Pushed the 13-commit remediation stack to Gerrit (changes 202-214), all with Change-Id + rebar-ticket trailers, rebased onto current origin/main. Full suite green (4267 passed; the 1 e2e editor failure is a pre-existing worktree-env issue — missing editor_assets/node_modules — verified identical at baseline). Merged already: 186/187/188 incl. the Critical has_llm_steps fix. 189 (child-closure docs) to re-push after the stack merges (Fix B/change 212 adds the .gitleaks.toml that clears its false-positive). Items 13/14/15/9.3 (config/reconcile splits, shared-helper sweep, dir reorg, facade reroute) CHECKPOINTED for a post-release maintenance pass.","timestamp":1783064499798729001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"MILESTONE: all 13 remediation changes (202-214) MERGED to main via Gerrit (two-bot gate: LLM-Review + Verified/CI), plus the earlier Critical has_llm_steps fix (188). One CI hiccup handled mid-flight: change 211 (Fix A) failed the mypy gate — a type-var issue in the new blocking-finding code (my gap: ran make lint but not make typecheck on the batch); fixed by str-coercing the file list, amended into 211, re-verified (mypy 246 files clean), re-pushed, merged. Change 189 (child-closure docs) re-pushed onto main-with-.gitleaks.toml: its LLM-Review block CLEARED (now +1) — end-to-end validation that the Fix A rendering bug + Fix B gitleaks allowlist resolved the false -1/0-findings vote. 189 CI finishing. Remaining epic children: 13/14/15/9.3 (config/reconcile splits, shared-helper sweep, dir reorg, facade reroute) — CHECKPOINTED for a post-release maintenance pass.","timestamp":1783069431088334001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"EPIC STATUS after this session: MERGED to main — the Critical has_llm_steps gate-bypass fix (188), the full 13-change remediation stack (202-214: bugs, gate hardening, reducer inversion, import-cycle guard, decompositions, dead code, the two 189 review-bot fixes), item 13 (config/reconcile/editor/batch_dispatch splits, 218-221), and item 14 (run_git/atomic_write/_reap/_lazy_load helpers, 225-228). ALL those child tickets are CLOSED. REMAINING (2): (a) item 9 part 3 / 9.3 facade-read reroute under ebd8 (lofty-flare-crest); (b) item 15 directory-reorg + TicketQuery under 6ae5 (toll-clock-tier). Both checkpointed for a post-release pass. Item 8 (allowlist governance) was REJECTED earlier (allowlist stays a record). Epic stays OPEN until 9.3 + item 15 land.","timestamp":1783083699419431001}],"created_at":1783053634713102001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"# Pre-release codebase-health remediations (2026-07-02 joe-janitor audit)\n\n## Context\n\nA verified codebase-health audit (joe-janitor, 2026-07-02: 8 concern agents + temporal\npass, then 4 adversarial verification agents; 0 findings refuted) ran ahead of next week's\nwider release. Full report at `.joe-janitor/report-2026-07-02.md`. Overall health is good and\nimproved since the 2026-06-24 audit, but a Critical gate-bypass, several High structural/governance\nitems, and a set of Mediums warrant remediation before increased external scrutiny.\n\nThis epic is the umbrella for the remediation work. Children are created per finding as they are\napproved; the Critical (risk 1) and the completion-gate doc drift (risk 2) are remediated first.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Risk 1 (has_llm_steps ALLOW_LLM bypass) remediated + regression test; child closed.\n- [ ] Risk 2 (completion-gate child-closure doc drift) remediated; child closed.\n- [ ] Stale-reference doc/comment fixes (already landed) tracked under a child.\n- [ ] The remaining approved remediations are decomposed into children, each with AC + file-impact.\n- [ ] All children closed with signed completion verdicts; report's Critical/High set addressed.\n- [ ] The Critical `ALLOW_LLM` gate bypass is fixed with a regression test; both shipped gate\n- [ ] Completion-gate docs match the post-`30c2ef3ad` child-closure semantics (blocking vs\n- [ ] Each approved remediation lands as its own child through Gerrit (LLM-Review + Verified),","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a64335d9-2f95-40a8-abe2-af41519db129","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9322-f84a-e047-4471","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Pre-release codebase-health remediations (2026-07-02 audit)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["118a728a-aeaa-4901-a3c5-b5484dc65542","1a88e56e-d39b-4cee-85ca-52586f175e81","3c42ddb7-f740-46a8-ba22-100ba9fd9f9e","4fef66c2-4d08-40c7-a40b-00b281fbce40","1754153d-5b3d-44e1-9aab-244955b1471d","74f7dcfd-80ab-4420-9a72-300b681e9d94","b80b2d84-4fb8-47d4-bc7f-bdbbfeb00226","a64335d9-2f95-40a8-abe2-af41519db129","b08a3bde-89cd-4722-85c6-323a23e78345","ff27e76f-506b-42f1-b999-59291d985644","e36af9a5-f48c-4903-a9d9-456ba62cbf02"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994012868786001,"uuid":"8787f523-b65c-424d-b987-bbb03606e8b0"}